title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.4

- Extensions Incorporated into SPIR-V 1.5:
* SPV_KHR_8bit_storage
* SPV_EXT_descriptor_indexing
* SPV_EXT_shader_viewport_index_layer, with changes:
  Replaced the single *ShaderViewportIndexLayerEXT* capability with the two new <<Capability, capabilities>>
  *ShaderViewportIndex* and *ShaderLayer*.
  Declaring both is equivalent to declaring *ShaderViewportIndexLayerEXT*.
* SPV_EXT_physical_storage_buffer and SPV_KHR_physical_storage_buffer
* SPV_KHR_vulkan_memory_model

- Khronos Issue #402: Relax <<OpGroupNonUniformBroadcast, *OpGroupNonUniformBroadcast*>> _Id_ from constant to
  dynamically uniform, starting with version 1.5.
- Khronos Issue #493: Relax <<OpGroupNonUniformQuadBroadcast, *OpGroupNonUniformQuadBroadcast*>> _Id_ from constant to
  dynamically uniform, starting with version 1.5.
- Khronos Issue #494: Update the <<DynamicallyUniform, _Dynamically Uniform_>> definition to say that the
  invocation group is the set of invocations, _unless otherwise stated_.
- Khronos Issue #485: When <<RelaxedPrecisionSection, RelaxedPrecision>> is applied to a numerical instruction, the
  operands may be truncated.
